## Definition

The terminal gts ARCHIVE writer \(the ONE canonical exit / narrow waist\): serialize the assembled carrier to generated/dist/gmeow\.gts\. GTS is exit\-only — produced here and nowhere else; every fold\-reading export leaf reads the carrier dataset off the gmeow:stage\-snapshot bundle, never these bytes\. The carrier is taken off the snapshot bundle \(no re\-assembly — the razor: transform transport→form at most once\)\. The eleven by\-reference TAR archives are READ off the gmeow:stage\-archive\-blobs product, folded once by that stage and never re\-folded here; the terminal staples only the blob channels it alone can see: the document\-scale language surface blobs, the native reasoning reports \(gmeow:stage\-reason\), the opaque generated/ fanout archive over THIS run's carrier, the typed SHACL/ShEx validation sidecars \(gmeow:stage\-compile\-logic\), and the SHACL diagnostics SARIF/findings \(gmeow:stage\-validate\)\. The embedded executable\-docs 'try it' surface reasons over the object\-level EDB, whose authored self\-description graphs ride on gmeow:stage\-source\-load \(read, never re\-loaded\)\. The opaque fanout members \(references, bench, agreement matrix, apache config, matrix, eval/research\-object sidecars, metadata void/dcat, the LinkML/TypeScript/GraphQL developer schema surfaces\) ride in from their producing export leaves — rendered once, in the leaf, never re\-rendered in the terminal \(the transform\-once razor\) It is also where the MEDIUM's dictionary\-effect measurement is taken and folded: the terminal is the one point at which the emission's whole BLOB frame set exists, so the two\-part code of every shipped dictionary \(gmeow:MediumDictionaryEffectMeasurement in graph/medium\-measurement, plus its graph/fanout twin for generated/medium/dictionary\-effect\.ttl\) is measured over exactly the frames it is about to write, on the mandated chain\. The SNAPSHOT frame is excluded from that population by declaration — the measurement lands in the snapshot payload, so pricing that frame would make the reading self\-referential — and that exclusion is permanent rather than a gap the two\-pass gmeow:envelopeDigestStratum fixpoint could close: the digest fixpoint converges only because gmeow:strataDigest is taken over a REGION that excludes the added records, while a compressed LENGTH has no such region \(compression is not additive over regions, so no proper sub\-region's length equals the frame's, and a length over 'the payload minus the measurement subgraph' would describe bytes the bundle never writes\)\. It is moot for the inventory in any case, because gmeow:payloadSchemaDictionary is maxQualifiedCardinality 1 and the snapshot schema binds exactly gmeow:dictGmeowCoreV1\. A dictionary that does not pay for itself stops the emission with gmeow:MediumDictionaryRegression rather than shipping\.

